The separate ReShikiOpsin adapter is original ReShiki code, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
It invokes OPSIN core locally, with strict pinned options, and adds no InChI/JNA
dependency. No OPSIN source has been modified. The Java runtime is a separately
installed prerequisite; ReShiki does not redistribute or download a JVM.

The official core distribution includes these dependency versions:

dk.brics:automaton 1.12-4 — BSD-3-Clause. Copyright Anders Moeller and
John Gibson. Full distinct upstream source headers are preserved with an
exact source-file index under automaton-1.12-4/.

com.fasterxml.woodstox:woodstox-core 7.1.1 — Apache-2.0. Upstream packaged
license declaration, POM and full release-tag license are retained under
woodstox-core-7.1.1/. The packaged declaration mentions Jackson databind;
its original bytes are retained rather than silently corrected.

net.java.dev.msv:xsdlib 2022.7 — BSD-3-Clause (Oracle/Sun), with bundled
regexp implementation notices under Apache Software License 1.1.
All six distinct source header texts, including the older Sun proprietary-
information attribution, and their exact file indices are preserved under
xsdlib-2022.7/. The upstream POM declares BSD. The project license does not
replace the per-file notices or Apache 1.1 terms.

com.sun.xml.bind.jaxb:isorelax 20090621 — MIT. Copyright Kohsuke Kawaguchi
and MURATA Makoto. All distinct source license/header notices and exact
file indices are retained under isorelax-20090621/.

org.codehaus.woodstox:stax2-api 4.2.2 — BSD-2-Clause. The packaged declaration
names FasterXML.com, 2010-. Its exact bytes and POM are retained alongside
the full upstream BSD-2-Clause terms (FasterXML LLC, 2008+) under stax2-api-4.2.2/.
The supplementary full-license source is separately pinned in
supplementary-license-sources.json; it supplements rather than replaces the
versioned artifact's original attribution.

commons-io:commons-io 2.21.0 and org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api 2.25.3 —
Apache-2.0. Their full packaged LICENSE and NOTICE files are retained in the
corresponding versioned folders.

dependencies.json records the seven exact source-artifact URLs, SHA256 values
and notice mappings. upstream.pom files retain their license declarations.
Binary packaging includes this directory through the existing notices
aggregator. ReShiki's project-level dual license does not relicense any of
these dependencies.
